    <string name="i18n_dictionary_moeDescription">Search Taiwanese Taigi and Mandarin, with audio for headwords and example sentences for easy learning. Includes category and radical-stroke indexes plus appendices.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_newwordDescription">Taigi TV invites experts and scholars to meet regularly, settle fitting Taigi terms for emerging words, and build a public lookup glossary.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_sttiDescription">Since 2017, the project has translated academic terminology from eight fields into Taigi: language arts, mathematics, social studies, natural science, arts, integrative activities, technology, and health and physical education.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_kunggeDescription">Over 1,200 key Taigi craft terms covering eleven categories such as ceramics, woodcraft, metalwork, bamboo and rattan, fiber, glass, lacquer, stonework, leather, and paper craft.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_lkkDescription">Suggested Han-Roman mixed-script characters from the Lí Kang-Khioh Taigi Culture and Education Foundation.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_devDescription">Adds government agencies, common names, administrative divisions, dates, times, numbers, and other words with limited coverage in the MOE Dictionary.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_iTaigiDescription">A crowd-edited open Taigi dictionary.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_taiwanJapanDescription">A Taigi dictionary compiled by Ogawa Naoyoshi during the Japanese era.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_taiHuaDescription">The Taiwanese–Mandarin Online Dictionary: data provided by Prof. Tīng Liông-uí, edited by Prof. Iûnn Ín-giân.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_taiwanPlantDescription">Taigi names for Taiwanese plants, compiled by Sasaki Shun\'ichi during the Japanese era.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_variantDescription">Marks Taigi variant characters based on MOE dictionary data.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_khpooDescription">Supplements regional accent differences.</string>
    <string name="i18n_dictionary_khiinDescription">Adds conventional characters used by Tsuí Tâi-bûn and Tâi-jī-tshân to candidate suggestions.</string>
